#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Write the Codex handoff for every house that is waiting on one.

Codex's own review: "The handoff is manual and not resumable ... Do not invent
another manual note format. Promote the existing handoff.json into a resumable
job contract." So this writes BOTH:

  codex-job.json      the contract: job id, every input .blend with its sha256,
                      the geometry/annotation hash it came from, the outputs
                      required and their state. Machine-checkable on return.
  CODEX-AUFTRAG.md    the same thing in German for a human, GENERATED from the
                      contract so the two cannot drift apart.

Resumable because each required output carries its own state: a rerun only
needs the entries that are still pending or failed. Idempotent: a house whose
job already matches the current .blend hashes is left alone.

    python make-codex-job.py --all
    python make-codex-job.py onehalfstorey_029
"""

import argparse
import datetime
import hashlib
import importlib.util
import json
import math
import os
